le online  calculator that takes all this  information it gives you a little  graphical output and helps you make a  decision about what type of nan legging  seeding rate to use what type of  nitrogen supply you'll get for your next  corn crop and this is described in a  paper that we have publishing actually  download just the HTML file everything  is embedded in that single file can  download that and and use the calculator  and we're working on getting some  tutorial videos  post it on on how to do that but it's an  attachment to this paper a supplement to  this paper you can download it now or  you can contact me for the file if  you're interested so conclusions  mixtures can increase multi  functionality but it requires intensive  management so functional diversity was  more important than species diversity  and our data shows that you should  target functional evenness and  divergence biomass evenness is a  challenge to achieve so you need to  select species with compatible growth  rates and adjust your seeding rates to  the climate and so on that nitrogen  status of your site and then services  are bundled and have trade-offs so to  minimize that nitrogen supply and  retention trade-off it's actually about  how you manage your soils so that was  kind of an interesting outcome from that  so I think that's all thank you I have  time for questions or okay a question or  two yes ma'am  after all  so that really varied depending on the  year and depending on the site so so  yeah that varied we took that we took  that into account by the c2n ratio so  that's essentially going to be a moving  target and in this calculator here we  actually have there's variables for your  spring growing degree days and your fall  growing degree days and those actually  shift the C to end ratio behind the  scenes in the model and so that can help  you account for some of that as well  yes  hmmm I think that there's still  something to the insurance effect of  having because yeah they